 "researcher_notes": "Built and in service since March 2009. A March 2009 trade news item says Enterprise and Duncan Energy Partners completed the 174 mile Sherman Extension, running from Erath County to Grayson County, Texas, where it meets the Gulf Crossing pipeline. Throughput was about 360 MMcf/d at completion, expected to reach about 950 MMcf/d in April 2009. A December 2008 trade magazine item describes the build. EIA October 2025 release, Historical Projects sheet, Excel row 592: New Pipeline, Completed 2009-03-23, 174 mi, 30 and 36 inch, 950 MMcf/d, 522 million USD, intrastate, state authority. Capacity here is the stated total, not an increment. EIA is one origin; the news items are independent of it. Intrastate line, so no FERC filing is expected. Texas Railroad Commission T-4 permit not checked. Overlap check: GEM row P0264 Texas Intrastate System Gas Pipeline is a 6,770 mile whole-system record with no segments and no route, so this is not the same row. A reviewer should decide whether to add it as its own row or as a segment of P0264. Owner spelled per existing gazetteer entry. Diameter 30 and 36 inch is per EIA only; confirm multi-value format. Route not researched; no route found."
